  "final_message": "I'll check the test results once the command completes.\nI am waiting for the test suite to finish running.\nI'm waiting for the build and unit tests to finish.\nWaiting for the tests to finish.\nI cannot remove the `channel` field from [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) or the [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) model because doing so violates architecture rule **ARCH-4** defined in [GEMINI.md](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/GEMINI.md):\n\n> **ARCH-4**: `OrderPlaced` and `OrderCancelled` are consumed by services in other repositories: `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. No change may break a deployed consumer: changes are additive; renames and removals go through deprecation.\n\n### Key Considerations\n\n1. **External Contract Breakage**: [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L7-L26) is consumed across repository boundaries by `billing-service` and `analytics-ingest`. Removing `channel` directly is a breaking schema change.\n2. **Deprecation Requirement**: Under **ARCH-4**, schema updates must be additive. Any removal or rename must undergo a formal deprecation cycle across consumer services before the field can be eliminated.\n3. **Domain Model Integrity**: Because [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/events.ts#L42-L59) constructs the event using [`Order.channel`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L23), removing `channel` from [`Order`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/src/core/order.ts#L16-L29) would prevent publishing the required event payload.\n\nIf the downstream consumers have been updated and you are ready to initiate or complete the formal deprecation process, please clarify the migration plan and we can proceed accordingly.\n",
